l this might also  create a hypoxic environment creating  metabolic stress and this could also  help you to engage more fast twitch  muscle fibers potentially as they're  anaerobic and need less oxygen if you've  hit a plateau and aesthetics are  important to you then going a bit more  slowly might just be what you're looking  for  another thing this does is it forces you  to control the movement all the way  through the repetition so if you're used  to exploding up out of the squat and you  might find that what you're actually  doing is allowing momentum to carry you  a lot of the way so you're not actually  required to put that much effort in at  the same time if you're just dropping  down then you're not really doing  anything either if you control the  movement and move up extremely slowly  like so and move down extremely slowly  then you're forced to control yourself  and to develop power and strength at  every point in the strength curve what i  find even more interesting about this is  that moving slowly allows you to focus  all your efforts on your slow twitch  muscle fiber the reason for this is that  fast twitch muscle fiber isn't capable  of moving something slowly the motor  units containing the fast twitch muscle  fiber are so big and powerful that they  represent a large step change in force  if you were to try and lift a spoon into  your mouth using fast switch muscle  fiber you'd smack yourself in the face  conversely the slower twitch muscle  fibers allow to add just that little bit  of extra force to gradually move  something towards you or away from you  this is why it's so much harder to move  something heavy slowly so  if i take this 20 kilogram dumbbell  and i try and slowly curl it  you're gonna see  that i really struggle  and have to put in a whole lot of effort  conversely if i do it quickly  then that's much easier because i can  explode through the movement by the way  guys you might have noticed that i'm  coming to you from a different l